    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nNestled within the charming and historic Old Russian Village in Kilquade, this exceptional c.0.5 acre plot offers a rare opportunity to create a home (subject to Planning Permission) in one of County Wicklow's most unique and picturesque settings. Surrounded by mature trees, established planting and the tranquillity of the countryside, Folio WW267F enjoys an atmosphere of peace and privacy that is increasingly difficult to find. \n\nThe Old Russian Village, renowned for its distinctive character and rich heritage, provides a truly special backdrop, appealing to those seeking a lifestyle defined by space, nature and a strong sense of place. The fascinating history is rooted in the city of Arkhangelsk, Russia. After the Bolshevik revolution in 1917, Bayan Giltsoff's family fled to London. Giltsoff became an architect and designed and built 20 houses here influenced by Russian dachas, which were small country estates. \n\nDespite its wonderfully secluded feel, the plot is conveniently positioned within easy reach of an excellent range of amenities including the renowned Arboretum café and garden centre a pleasant stroll away. Delgany and Greystones are just a short drive away, offering an array of cafés, restaurants, boutique shopping, schools and sporting facilities, while the nearby N11 provides swift access to Dublin and surrounding areas. For outdoor enthusiasts, the Wicklow countryside, coastal walks and numerous recreational amenities are all close at hand. Combining the charm of a historic setting with the convenience of modern-day connectivity, this is a unique opportunity to enjoy the very best of country living in a highly sought-after North Wicklow location."
      },
